  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency live saving WASH services to vulnerable people in Jonglei, South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will respond to the increasing humanitarian needs caused by the elevated food insecurity, flooding, displacement, and renewed conflicts to the affected host communities, Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs), and returnees through deployment of Emergency Rapid Response Teams (ERRT). Oxfam will respond through distribution of Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) minimum package items to promote access to safe water which will comprise distribution of WASH emergency kits including point -of -use water purification items and storage containers. Construction of dignified and inclusive climate resilient emergency latrines and installing bathing shelters is part of the project of the project intervention to prevent and curb open defecation practices and improved hygiene practices. Oxfam will be directly implementing the project through the Emergency Rapid Response Teams (ERRT).</narrative>
  </description>
